{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/channel.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731748Z","id":"4643b8805198331cfd586ef4c720626da877005020b1d2d06bf4883a5b223513","body":{"detail":"channel_events(within) collects for the whole window; the negative checks (lines 387, 425, 476) pay it in full on purpose.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":177},"content_hash":"143d09c57b3760bfb6f63632c6fd6fd946ce15eeeab169ff23e251a9db9078ca"},"summary":"The channel tests wait 3 to 5 s windows to show no second event arrives","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/common.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731776Z","id":"b42d4ebfa66df83f60c7952b63600300af453be578868ad719498bbe400d1897","body":{"detail":"With CLAX_TEST_BIN unset, clax_bin builds clax once per process, and under nextest each test is a process, so each build replaces target/debug/clax while other tests run it. The same fallback is in crates/clax-hooks/tests/golden.rs:13-37. just test and the gates set CLAX_TEST_BIN.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":40},"content_hash":"2f5d33d51f0897726481ac38e2e851d02c82deab59fd8c48d6ffcaa7fe5ff839"},"suggested_fix":"A nextest setup script that sets CLAX_TEST_BIN, once that feature is stable.","summary":"A bare cargo nextest run races on target/debug/clax","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/common.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:06:13.534619Z","id":"4b2a4b22b89354139a88d2fc937ad057089716704044def190d0138e8d81ad75","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:aac4e8e9","summary":"Fixed: crates/clax-mcp/tests/common.rs is gone; clax-mcp, clax-hooks, clax-server and clax-cli tests take clax from clax_fake_exe::clax_bin (crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs), which runs a stable-bin.sh copy kept by content, never target/debug/clax in place. Evidence: 'env -u CLAX_TEST_BIN cargo nextest run -p clax-mcp -p clax-hooks -p clax-cli -p clax-fake-exe --no-fail-fast' -> 'Summary [77.790s] 552 tests run: 552 passed, 1 skipped'; 'env -u CLAX_TEST_BIN cargo test -p clax-mcp --test integration open_status' -> '1 passed'.","supersedes":"b42d4ebfa66df83f60c7952b63600300af453be578868ad719498bbe400d1897","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:01.003810Z","id":"3ed41f13e18cd340f271e7778cdbda9c9df23abf6b3f2d111e39bf6e1691d173","body":{"detail":"browser_thread (a multipart POST /api/artifacts/<raid>/threads with the public instance's cookie, Host and Origin) is here, in crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs:36 and in crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:2220 (browser_thread_on); all three drive clax_testkit::remotes::Public. async fn agent(ts) -> ClaxTools (register a session, build DaemonClient and ClaxTools) is repeated in crates/clax-mcp/tests/connect_instance.rs:14, remote_artifacts.rs:19, publish_public.rs:71 and site_access.rs:12. clax-testkit may depend on clax-mcp (SERVER includes MCP in scripts/check-crate-layers.py).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":48},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"42441812f14c02ecff79a0b28553d0796e068b257d3d1b047487216d3f438d79"},"suggested_fix":"Add Public::browser_thread(raid, cookie, anchor, body) -> Value to crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs and delete the three copies; add one agent-tools helper (in clax-testkit, or a tests/common module in clax-mcp) for the ClaxTools setup.","summary":"The browser-thread test helper is now copied in three test files, and the ClaxTools agent setup in four","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","tests","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:28:55.926999Z","id":"c82db36a1982179587e2d8b3e6085d5fddeced5847e4f92d7c1c7db41aa731c1","body":{"detail":"The same multipart POST with Public's cookie, Host and Origin is at crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs:48-70, crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs:34-56 and crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:2224-2244 (browser_thread_on); they differ only in anchor, cookie source and return value. agent(ts) is identical apart from the session name in crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs:19-28, connect_instance.rs:14-22, publish_public.rs:71-79 and site_access.rs:12-20. scripts/check-crate-layers.py:77 allows clax-testkit SERVER, which includes MCP (line 51), so the helper can live in clax-testkit.","kind":"comment","references":"3ed41f13e18cd340f271e7778cdbda9c9df23abf6b3f2d111e39bf6e1691d173","summary":"confirmed: browser_thread is copied in three test files and the ClaxTools agent setup in four","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T06:16:49.960451Z","id":"e724722f0edbf78696fdfadcf8c88635d3c0759a691757943cb30c3e9ca13864","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:43aa70f60","summary":"Public::browser_thread (crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs) and clax_testkit::mcp::agent_tools replace the three browser_thread copies (crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs, crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs, crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs browser_thread_on) and the four agent(ts) helpers (connect_instance.rs, remote_artifacts.rs, publish_public.rs, site_access.rs). bazelisk test //crates/clax-mcp:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-testkit:all: 11 of 11 pass.","supersedes":"3ed41f13e18cd340f271e7778cdbda9c9df23abf6b3f2d111e39bf6e1691d173","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T19:14:51.926286Z","id":"daa43a18b9b896d9529b04e77446597cc545d7af63d0bb85c6fba4ebf5f8948f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e724722f0edbf78696fdfadcf8c88635d3c0759a691757943cb30c3e9ca13864","summary":"Commit 43aa70f60 cited by this close was re-signed as bc3970641 (same tree, author and message).","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/comments.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:02:03.132272Z","id":"eb424259fd34f218d18e2f35c7ab690615f532a611ca159c01a805f9f132c1b4","body":{"detail":"The test posts POST /api/sessions/<sid>/working/end and drops the response (ts.post_json does not check status, crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs:1089-1098), and the record held only the background thread, so the assertion at 885 that it still names that thread is also what a failed or no-op turn end leaves. The test therefore does not show the turn end ran or that it spares background threads; it also never checks `thread_ids: []` with `background: true`, the other branch of the new validation in do_working (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:3107-3113).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":877},"end":{"line":885},"content_hash":"e37df65e7ea6cce0268095dfda52adea61136900b60e378a6c052eff1336e1e2"},"suggested_fix":"Assert the turn end's status, have the record also name a foreground thread before it and assert that thread is gone afterwards; add `thread_ids: Some(vec![])` with `background: Some(true)` to the refused cases.","summary":"working_in_the_background_keeps_threads_past_the_turn_end passes even if the turn end failed or cleared nothing","tags":["review","review:pr-90","session:claude-code:ee9b76d4-2000-4639-9c8f-6a12a16119a5"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/comments.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:05:56.693495Z","id":"32845b9400cf94354008998ba1772cf62e8583bdd2ce1e235c37b88657c89177","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/tests/comments.rs:877-878 calls ts.post_json and ignores the Response (no status check, crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs:1089-1098); the record names only the background tid (set at comments.rs:864-875), so the assertion at comments.rs:885 is what a failed or no-op turn end also leaves. The refused cases (comments.rs:891-904) are background without thread_ids and background with done; `thread_ids: Some(vec![])` with `background: Some(true)`, the second half of the check at crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:3111-3113, is not exercised (the route's own check is covered by crates/clax-server/tests/api_working.rs:395).","kind":"comment","references":"eb424259fd34f218d18e2f35c7ab690615f532a611ca159c01a805f9f132c1b4","span":{"start":{"line":877},"end":{"line":885},"content_hash":"e37df65e7ea6cce0268095dfda52adea61136900b60e378a6c052eff1336e1e2"},"summary":"confirmed: the turn end's response is dropped, the record has no foreground thread, and the empty thread_ids case is not refused in this test","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:ee9b76d4-2000-4639-9c8f-6a12a16119a5"]}}
